edits_description = " The text and huts where removed, a cloak was recolored, and the image was cropped."
final_image_tex = SubResource("Resource_jg17w")
province = 54
blurb = "Depicts a rainy scene of the Suzuka Pass near Tsuchiyama (in present-day Shiga prefecture), an area which was known to be unusually rainy.

Like the rest of the prints in this series, it has a kyōka (comic poem) inscribed:

[i]Even if you are in a hurry,
go with caution.
If you slip,
you will slide back down
rainy Tsuchiyama.[/i]

The attribution next to the poem states \"Teahouse Girl at the Brushwood Gate\", not a specific real poet, suggesting that this is generic advice given by someone at a tea house rest stop along the Tōkaidō."
metadata/_custom_type_script = "uid://6kpsqyb2pk7a"
